		{"id":"577b713459b4c964","type":"text","text":"[[Insula Nefanda.canvas]]\n#WildFort","x":-125,"y":-30,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"6da458d1c8177a94","x":-125,"y":60,"width":551,"height":253,"type":"text","text":"A hall of dusty old tomes none that have any real value but they all seem to have been left untouched for a very very long time. \n\nThe hallway extends for a few hundred feet before opening to a large Hexagonal chamber.\n\nIn the center a cauldron stained with blood and on the far wall a stone plaque written in sigils that reads. \"Pour yourself and tell no story of the secrets that lay below\"\n\nᛔᚮᚢᚱ ᚤᚮᚢᚱᛍᛂᛚᚠ ᛆᚿᛑ ᛐᛂᛚᛚ ᚿᚮ ᛍᛐᚮᚱᚤ ᚮᚠ Þᛂ ᛍᛂᛌᚱᛂᛐᛍ Þᛆᛐ ᛚᛆᚤ ᛒᛂᛚᚮᚡ\n\nWhen a person pours their blood into the cauldron the stone wall underneath the plaque will slowly rise into the ceiling revealing a dark rocky and jagged cavern that is illuminated by torch light curving through the ground to the right\n\nGreen immortal Salamander that shanks you for 10d6 if you grab a book\n"}
	],
	"edges":[]
}